From: Robin <robin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] WTF MemoryPressureHandler: do not repeat the memory relief on every poll

measurementTimerFired() runs releaseMemory() on every poll while the footprint is above the conservative or strict
threshold. WebKit polls every 30 s by default; Robin polls every 2 s (so a runaway web process is seen before the TV
runs out of memory) with thresholds of 182 MB / 286 MB, which most real pages exceed. On the TV that was a relief every
2 s: the engine log showed a "Memory pressure relief" line every 2 s through Speedometer and on Wikipedia, and each
strict relief throws away all JIT code, every document's style data and the decoded images, and starts a GC.

The relief now runs when the policy becomes stricter (Unrestricted -> Conservative -> Strict) and is repeated only after
MEMORY_RELIEF_REPEAT_S seconds (default 30, 0 = on every poll as before). The kill check (with 0027's consecutive-poll
rule) still runs on every poll.
---
diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/MemoryPressureHandler.cpp b/Source/WTF/wtf/MemoryPressureHandler.cpp
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/MemoryPressureHandler.cpp
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/MemoryPressureHandler.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include <wtf/Logging.h>
 #include <wtf/MathExtras.h>
 #include <wtf/MemoryFootprint.h>
+#include <wtf/MonotonicTime.h>
 #include <wtf/NeverDestroyed.h>
 #include <wtf/RAMSize.h>
 
@@ -245,6 +246,26 @@
 }
 
 
+// The relief that runs while the footprint stays above a threshold is expensive: Strict throws away all JIT code, every
+// document's style data and the decoded images, and starts a GC; Conservative clears the selector, font and layout caches.
+// WebKit repeats it on every poll. With a short poll interval (a TV browser polls every 2 s so the kill threshold is seen
+// in time) that is a purge every 2 s for any page above the conservative threshold. Now the relief runs when the policy
+// becomes stricter, and is repeated only after MEMORY_RELIEF_REPEAT_S seconds (default 30, WebKit's own poll interval;
+// 0 = every poll, the old behaviour). The kill check still runs on every poll.
+static Seconds memoryReliefRepeatInterval()
+{
+    static const Seconds interval = [] {
+        if (const char* value = getenv("MEMORY_RELIEF_REPEAT_S")) {
+            char* end = nullptr;
+            double seconds = strtod(value, &end);
+            if (end != value && seconds >= 0 && seconds <= 3600)
+                return Seconds(seconds);
+        }
+        return 30_s;
+    }();
+    return interval;
+}
+
 void MemoryPressureHandler::measurementTimerFired()
 {
     size_t footprint = memoryFootprint();
@@ -264,8 +285,19 @@
     }
 
     m_consecutivePollsAboveKillThreshold = 0;
+    auto previousPolicy = m_memoryUsagePolicy;
     setMemoryUsagePolicyBasedOnFootprint(footprint);
 
+    static MonotonicTime lastRelief;
+    if (m_memoryUsagePolicy == MemoryUsagePolicy::Unrestricted)
+        lastRelief = { };
+    else {
+        auto now = MonotonicTime::now();
+        if (m_memoryUsagePolicy <= previousPolicy && lastRelief && now - lastRelief < memoryReliefRepeatInterval())
+            return;
+        lastRelief = now;
+    }
+
     switch (m_memoryUsagePolicy) {
     case MemoryUsagePolicy::Unrestricted:
         break;
